From ac052938b61d367253d353d81ab4ac077b4178e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:54:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Target-type a set! value through deref and aref places
 (nuc-iron-doom ISSUE-009)

(set! @p (some 4)) with p:&?i32 died with "some: value must be non-null",
and (set! @p none) with a type mismatch, though a field place and a named
local build the arm against the place's type. The deref and aref set!
paths now emit their value through emit-place-value, which arms the want
channel and applies union-target-rewrite as the other two paths do.

Test: doom-place-target-types-maybe.
Gate: 1675 pass, the same 4 suite-build AVR failures; bootstrap PASS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8hzrZakM3KWb32SpqKh
